\item \strong{B. Positivity audit}: \emph{continuous sensitivity intervals}
for the censoring mechanism (tilting-based), plus detectable positivity
sub-problems (sparse tail risk sets). By design this dimension does
\emph{not} emit green/yellow/red verdicts on the censoring mechanism,
because independence of censoring is not directly testable.
\item \strong{C. Extrapolation audit}: three-model comparison
(Royston-Parmar 2-knot spline / standard parametric / constant-tail),
\eqn{\rho} instability and maturity criteria, and a configurable
mapping to PSA strategies for HTA use.
}

\strong{Two-step discipline (project governance)}: this Phase A package
makes \emph{no} claim of statistical performance superiority over manually
chaining single-dimension tools. The cross-dimensional interaction pathway
(argument \code{.interaction} in \code{\link{depcens_audit}}) is a frozen
interface reserved for the Phase B methodology release; passing a non-NULL
value is an error in this version.

\strong{Wording discipline}: all outputs are diagnostic ("data support is
insufficient to constrain tail behaviour"), never adjudicative.
